262 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/E (This project focuses on the creation and evaluation of a composite material made from Aloe vera fibers, combined with epoxy resin and hardener. Aloe vera fibers, known for their natural strength, lightweight properties, and environmental friendliness, were chosen as the reinforcing material. The epoxy resin serves as the binding matrix, while the hardener facilitates the curing process to form a solid, durable composite. The primary objective of this project is to explore the mechanical properties of the resulting composite, including tensile strength, flexural strength, and impact resistance, and to determine how these properties vary with different fiber orientations and resin-to-hardener ratios. The project also aims to assess the potential applications of this sustainable composite material in various industries, such as automotive, construction, and consumer goods. Through this research, Aloe vera fiber-reinforced epoxy composites are positioned as an eco-friendly alternative to conventional synthetic composites, offering both environmental and performance benefits.)
/Pg 11 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
