/E (NFRCs can be developed using thermoset as well as thermoplastic material. Thermoplastic contain linear or branched polymeric chain. Therefore, it has tendency to soften after heating and return to its original state after cooling. Whereas, thermosets composed of crosslink and network type polymeric chain. It requires heat for curing. Once thermoset cured, it cannot achieve its initial state. Therefore, primary processing of both types of polymers are different. Thermoset based NFRCs can be processed with hand lay-up, resin transfer molding, vacuum bag molding, pultrusion, filament winding and compression molding. Hand lay-up process can be used for any form of fiber like short furlong fiber, particulate type fiber, unidirectional fiber, bidirectional fiber a woven type fiber. )
